## Goal
Flag empty `catch { }` bodies the same way the game-side compiler does.

## Source
todo-cover-cases-next.txt — Case 1 (2026-04-20, tm-control-mcp)

## Repro
```angelscript
try { x = something(); } catch { }
```

## Compiler (game-side)
`ManialinkIntrospection.as (73, 17) : error: expected declaration, found RBrace`
(cascades for ~40 diagnostics when nested inside control flow)

## Workaround
Put at least one token in the catch body, e.g. `catch { /* swallow */ }`

## Acceptance
- [ ] Empty catch body emits a diagnostic
- [ ] Non-empty catch (stmt or comment-only if AS requires a real stmt) behaves correctly
- [ ] Regression test for empty catch

## Notes
LSP today does not flag empty catch bodies.